From: Richard T. Carback III <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: wcd9378-sdca: Do not halve the TX host clock

The probe sets HOST_CLK_DIV2_CTL (SCP 0xf0, bank 1 copy) to 1 and
commits it. With the swr2 DP2 configuration used for the headset
microphone (sample interval 2, one-bit words) the codec has to run its
TX path from the undivided host clock: when the active bank holds 1,
no capture ever delivers data; with 0 in both banks capture works. The
bank 0 copy (0xe0) is already 0 after reset, so only streams that run
in bank 1 were affected.

Drop the write and the SCP_COMMIT that went with it, so that both
banks keep the reset value 0.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
index 37a666bca..ab03e0b4f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
@@ -862,9 +862,6 @@ static struct sdca_function_data wcd9378_sdca_data = {
 	.reset_max_delay  = 25000, /* 25ms — WCD9378 power-on reset completes well within this */
 };
 
-/* Vendor SCP register: host clock divide-by-2 (bank 1 shadow). */
-#define WCD9378_SCP_HOST_CLK_DIV2_CTL_B1	0xf0
-
 #define WCD9378_ANA_MBHC_MECH_ADDR		0x40180014
 #define WCD9378_ANA_MBHC_MECH_ENABLE		0xB5
 #define WCD9378_ANA_MBHC_MECH_DET_TYP		0x20
@@ -1126,19 +1123,6 @@ int wcd9378_sdca_probe(struct sdw_slave *slave,
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
 				     "slave attach timeout: %d\n", ret);
 
-	/*
-	 * TX PDM clock: bank-1 shadow + SCP_COMMIT.  SCP survives PDE
-	 * cycles; one-shot before any port is enabled.
-	 */
-	ret = sdw_write_no_pm(slave, WCD9378_SCP_HOST_CLK_DIV2_CTL_B1, 0x01);
-	if (ret)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
-				     "HOST_CLK_DIV2_CTL_B1: %d\n", ret);
-
-	ret = sdw_write_no_pm(slave, SDW_SCP_COMMIT, 0x02);
-	if (ret)
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "SCP_COMMIT: %d\n", ret);
-
 	/* DT has no DisCo enumeration; seed the descriptor here. */
 	if (!data->num_functions) {
 		data->function[0].type = wcd9378_sdca_desc.type;
